==Development==
During the development of ''{{smw|Super Mario 64}}'', the development team had plans to include a horse, which were later moved to {{OoT|-}}. The developers did not want controls to be difficult, so Epona was made to automatically jump over barriers if she has enough speed. To make the experience more entertaining, the carrot system was established, as well as mounted archery. The developers also wanted to include one-on-one battles and horseback swordplay, though such features did not appear until {{TP|-}}. 

The scene where Epona jumps over the broken bridge in Gerudo Valley was specially requested by [[Shigeru Miyamoto]]. A similar scene is shown when Epona escapes from Lon Lon Ranch, which had more than one exit, so a cutscene was made for each. The idea of horses and these scenes were inspired by Western movies.<ref name="IwataAsks">{{Cite Web|url= http://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/3ds/zelda-ocarina-of-time/1/4|title= What We Couldn't Do with The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time|site= Nintendo official website}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Web|url= http://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/3ds/zelda-ocarina-of-time/4/2|title= Everyone Loves Horses|site= Nintendo official website}}</ref>

==Trivia==
*Various unnamed horses resembling Epona appear in the opening cinematics of {{OoS}}, {{OoA}}, and {{TWW}}, as well as in [[The Field]] stage from {{FSA}}.
*During development of {{OoT|-}}, Link would use a whip to control Epona. After using the whip, Link would have to give her a carrot.<ref>{{Cite Web|quote= '''Q: How do you control the horse?'''<br/>'''Miyamoto:''' With whips and carrots. For each time you use the whip, you have to give the horse a carrot. If you only use the whip, then we'd feel sorry for the horse.|author= |published= November 26, 1997|retrieved= March 26, 2016|url= http://www.ign.com/articles/1997/11/27/the-z-files-4|title= The Z-Files|site= IGN|type=}}</ref>
*In {{BotW|-}}, it is possible to have multiple copies of Epona registered with the [[Stable Association]]. Whenever Epona is summoned with the appropriate [[amiibo]], she can be registered as one of Link's horses. There is no limit to how many Eponas can be summoned and registered from different copies of the appropriate amiibo. The same is true for {{TotK|-}}.
*Any copies of Epona registered in a {{BotW|-}} save file will be carried over to {{TotK|-}} once Link speaks to any Stable owner.

==Nomenclature==
{{wp|Epona}} is named after the Celtic Goddess of horses and fertility.<ref name="IwataAsks"/> It is built from the Celtic word ''epos'', meaning "horse".<ref>{{Cite Web|published= January 21, 2022 |retrieved= January 15, 2023 |url= https://www.behindthename.com/name/epona |archive= https://web.archive.org/web/20221216203213/https://www.behindthename.com/name/epona |title= Meaning, origin and history of the name Epona |site= Behind the Name}}</ref>

